Whenever you convey the Program or a modified version in object code form, you must make the complete Corresponding Source available to all recipients. The Corresponding Source must be available on a network server or other publicly accessible means at no more than the cost of physical distribution, and must remain available for at least 12 months after your last distribution.

**5.4** The Corresponding Source must include:
- All source code files;
- Build scripts, makefiles, and configuration files;
- Interface definition files;
- Documentation describing how to compile, install, and run the modified version.

**5.5** The Corresponding Source must be provided in a widely-used, machine-readable format (e.g., .zip, .tar.gz) and must require no special password, key, or proprietary software for unpacking, reading, or copying.

**5.6** If you convey the Program in source code form, you may satisfy the requirements of this Section by providing a copy of the source code along with the distribution, or by directing recipients to a publicly accessible network server where the source code is available.

**5.7** **Official Source Reference:**
When referring to the original source code in §3.4, you may refer to the Official Project Repository or any successor location publicly designated by the Original Author.

