### 6. Termination and Revocation

**6.1** **General Termination for Breach:**
A violation of this License may result in termination of the rights granted herein. Material Breaches are subject to the immediate-revocation provisions of Section 6.2. Non-Material Breaches are subject to the notice and cure procedure in Section 6.3. Any attempt to propagate or modify a covered work outside the terms of this License is void.

**6.2** **Specific Grounds for Immediate Revocation (Material Breach):**
The Original Author may revoke your license immediately—without prior notice or cure period—if you engage in a Material Breach, including:

- **(a) Plagiaristic Resale** (as defined in Section 0.12), including removing attribution or renaming the Program to imply original authorship;
- **(b) A violation of Section 1** (Copyright and Attribution), such as obscuring or removing copyright notices;
- **(c) A violation of Section 4** (Restricted Content), specifically using the Program to create, host, or distribute content that constitutes a Material Breach of the Restricted Content definitions.

**6.3** **Cure Period for Non-Material Breaches:**
For breaches other than Material Breaches listed in Section 6.2, the Original Author will provide written notice to you specifying the nature of the breach. You will have a period of thirty (30) days from receipt of such notice to cure the breach. If you cure the breach within this period, your license is reinstated. If you fail to cure, the license terminates permanently.

**6.4** **Reinstatement:**
If your license is terminated for a non-material breach and you cure it, your license is permanently reinstated. If your license is terminated for a Material Breach listed in Section 6.2, it is permanently revoked and may not be reinstated.

**6.5** **Protection for Innocent Downstream Recipients:**
Termination or revocation of your license does not terminate the licenses of parties who have received copies or rights from you under this License, provided they are in full compliance with this License. The Original Author's rights are preserved against you, but innocent downstream recipients are protected.

**6.6** Upon termination or revocation, you must immediately cease exercising the rights granted by this License and, to the extent reasonably practicable and permitted by applicable law, remove or destroy all copies under your control, including modified versions. Automated Backups that are not intended for active distribution or use are exempt from this destruction requirement, provided they are not used in any manner inconsistent with this License.

**6.7** **Limitation on Revocation:**
The Original Author's right to revoke the license is limited to the specific grounds set forth in this Section 6. Revocation shall be made in writing, specifying the grounds for revocation with reasonable particularity.

